From 954030641884f5d371232e2d2db580cebfee3250 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakshay <lakshay810bansal@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:16:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] HBF attach 3 (structural H3), GPU
 credit/deadlock/Ramulator front-end options

-gpgpu_hbf_attach 3 models H3 with an unmodified GPU. The GPU has no tier
check: memory_config::gpu_routes_hbf() is false, so every L2 miss is cached,
takes the L2->DRAM queue and the partition's DRAM credits, and crosses the
GPU<->HBM link (token bucket of -gpgpu_hbf_phy_gbps charging write payload
down and read data up, for both tiers). h3_dram_cycle() replaces dram_cycle():
the GPU MC feeds the HBM base die's ingress FIFO, whose router sends HBM
addresses to the HBM controller and HBF addresses through the GPU front end
(a latency pipeline) and a D2D queue (-gpgpu_hbf_h3_queue_size) to the HBF
stack. Replies return through the base die and the link.
- -gpgpu_hbf_d2d_hop[_ns]: D2D round trip added to every NAND operation;
  LHB hits (LHB in the HBM base die) skip it and the HBF channel link
- -gpgpu_hbf_h3_{issues,admits,returns}_per_tick (default 1)
- attach 3 needs one stack, no page cache, an HBF window and the DRAM model
- stats: base-die routing, router stalls, credit max/limit, link bytes

Also:
- attach 0: HBF requests can pay -gpgpu_hbf_frontend_latency_ns in a
  pipeline bounded by the DRAM credits (0 keeps the old path exactly)
- -gpgpu_dram_max_outstanding: GPU-side DRAM credits per partition
- -gpgpu_ramulator_frontend_pipeline: only requests past Ramulator's fixed
  front-end latency count against the bridge buffer
- -gpgpu_deadlock_window: deadlock check interval in cycles

Every new option defaults to the earlier behaviour. Attach 0/1/2 runs of the
earlier routing validation, and vectorAdd C1-C4 of hbfsim_4arch, reproduce
to the cycle.
